# The /vehicles "Neith" experience media (build-sequence frames, gallery
# videos, 3D models, component photos) is committed as normal git objects
# under public/vehicle/, the same way the gallery and blog media are stored.
#
# It used to be tracked through Git LFS, but the deploy host (Vercel) serves
# the LFS pointer files rather than the binaries unless LFS is explicitly
# enabled, which left the vehicle page with no media. Committing the real
# bytes makes it deploy anywhere, exactly like every other page's media.
